WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.160
It was Chin's great assault
on the Kingdom of Gi:

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.790
With their victory in the very first battle,

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:50.000
the Chin army's offensive
was off to a good start.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.870
However, no one realized at the time

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.700
that further on down the road,

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:01.250
they would be facing off against
an unthinkably huge opponent.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.040
Those Chin mongrels have invaded our land,

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.040
and now even Kyo Chu and Kyo Sai have fallen.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.580
And yet,

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:18.790
my heart remains free from terror--
because <i>you</i> are here.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.660
Formerly of Sho's Three Greats...

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.790
General Ren Pa!

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:30.080
In the three years you have
been exiled to our land,

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.290
never before have I been
so grateful for your presence!

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.000
"The Man Ren Pa"

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.370
It was the same year as Shin's first campaign,

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.450
the battle of Dakan Plain:

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:52.660
that mighty clash between
Lord Hyou of Chin and Go Kei of Gi.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:58.290
Some months earlier, another grand battle
was taking place elsewhere.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:21.250
Recorded in the Shiki annals,
this battle was especially unusual,

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.370
even for the Spring and Autumn period,

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:29.410
for the Sho army was fighting against itself.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:44.700
"Ren Pa: One of
 Sho's Three Greats"

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.870
The Three Greats were three skilled generals,
the pride of Sho.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:56.330
As heroic as Ou Ki and
the rest of Chin's six great generals,

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:58.950
they were known
throughout the Middle Kingdom

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.910
for their tremendous military prowess
and battle records.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.870
One of these Three Greats was Ren Pa.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.450
Ren Pa is coming! Stop him!

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:18.750
Wh-What's going on?
That's the Sho army--same as us!

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:23.870
Worse, isn't Ren Pa a great
general--and a Sho hero?

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.500
How did it come to this?

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.160
General Ren Pa shows no sign of stopping!

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.870
Dammit! If this keeps up, Gaku Jou, sir...

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:38.870
Stand firm!

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:43.380
"Gaku Jou, 
General of Sho"

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:40.870
Send the Fourth Brigade

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:42.910
into the left flank and break it up.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.080
Sir!

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.620
We fought together for twenty years.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:52.620
I have Ren Pa's fighting style memorized.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.660
That's General Gaku Jou for you!

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.700
We've got this one!

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:01.330
General Ren Pa...
what on earth are you thinking?

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.160
This unusual battle of ally versus ally
had its beginnings

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:11.080
earlier that year, when King Tou Jou
took the throne.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.620
Badly behaved since his time as crown prince,

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.160
King Tou Jou was often admonished by Ren Pa.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:23.040
The twisted King bore a deep-rooted
grudge against him for this,

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.290
and as soon as he took the throne,
he sent word to Ren Pa

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:29.370
stripping him of his rank
as general mid-campaign.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:34.500
Naturally, Ren Pa refused
this irrational shakeup.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:39.870
Furious, King Tou Jou
mustered an army of fifty thousand,

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:43.660
and ordered Gaku Jou
to go after the traitorous Ren Pa.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:49.160
Gaku Jou was of Gaku Ki's clan,
a genius on a level with

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.950
the great strategist Sho Katsu Komei.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:56.200
Gaku Jou was Sho's
second general after Ren Pa;

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:01.540
it was rumored that his abilities
actually outshone Ren Pa's in battle.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.450
General Ren Pa.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:13.790
Absurd though it may be,
these are the King's orders.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:17.830
Please hand your men over to me
and return to Kantan.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:21.620
General...

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:28.910
If you don't comply, I shall have
to take you to Kantan by force.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:32.540
And you think you can do that, do you?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.830
I don't want to, but if I must...

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:43.330
You have eight thousand men
to our fifty thousand.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:45.540
You have no means of resisting them.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.290
How amusing.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:53.500
I will <i>make</i> the means. Prepare yourself.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.620
General, please, wait!

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:00.370
Don't you know what could happen to you
if you go through with this?

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:07.040
I struggle to comprehend why
he would do something so foolish...

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.410
Has he thought of something?

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.330
But it's already too late...

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:20.080
Once we have crossed swords,
I, Gaku Jou, shall show no mercy.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:33.700
The central unit under Ren Pa has collapsed!
It's collapsed!

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:36.120
So Ren Pa's unit is gone?

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:36.950
There we go!

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.500
General Ren Pa is slain!

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.950
Gaku Jou's army is the mightiest in Sh--

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.790
Well, Gaku Jou? Had enough?

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.160
I...

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:06.330
I yield.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.200
That's what I thought!

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:14.410
Hand 'em over!

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:19.870
General Ren Pa! What you're doing here--
it's insanity!

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:22.660
You won't be able to return to Sho like this!

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:25.660
Ah, but I have no intention of returning!

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:30.250
King Tou Jou... he's no good.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:33.700
The last King was all right,
but this one is unbearable.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:38.200
And there is nothing more foolish
than working for a fool!

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.000
Ren Pa, sir!

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.540
He can't mean to abandon his country!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.410
I am disappointed!

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.950
Does it mean so little to you,

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:54.000
everything you've built as general?

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:59.080
Do your feelings toward Sho
mean so very little?!

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:08.910
My feelings toward war mean far more!

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:18.790
It was war that raised me. War made me
famous and led me to mighty foes,

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:22.870
foes I battled with all my body and soul.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:25.410
War is my everything!

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.200
And he...

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:31.330
he would strip me of my rank?!

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:34.870
He may as well be flinging mud
onto the sacred battlefield!

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:36.200
That imbecile King!

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.660
And the retainers who permitted this--
fools, the lot of 'em!

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:41.160
Has the Royal Court become
a meeting-place for swine?!

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.290
Gaku Jou...

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:52.580
You put up a good fight.
Even made me sweat a time or two.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:56.290
Which is all well and good, but...

00:09:56.290 --> 00:10:01.450
Compared to those Chin bastards,
that only keeps me about eighty--

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.830
no, sixty percent satisfied.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:10.580
The battlefield's just not
the same without them...

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:21.580
It seems he's always been
in a different league than these men...

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:27.750
And so Ren Pa brought
his surviving officers with him

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.660
as he exiled himself to Gi.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.500
In the three years since,
Ren Pa had not once

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:36.790
even tried to lead the Gi army.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:41.870
However...

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.790
now the great general had raised the Gi flag

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:47.040
and expressed his intention
to return to the battlefield.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:54.200
The fierce general Ren Pa,
who as one of Sho's Three Greats

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:59.000
was on a par with Chin's Ou Ki
and his fellow six great generals,

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.620
now had in his sights
the Chin army under Mou Gou,

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.160
currently invading the land of Gi.

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:13.750
We've been waiting for you, my lord.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:20.120
You lot! I should've known. Sniffed me out, eh?

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:24.620
Pretty rotten, not coming
to us Big Four for advice!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.910
You don't seem any less happy for that omission.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:33.870
Indeed! Why, to see your
imposing figure in action

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:37.450
would make my heart leap--
I would be walking on air.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:39.580
Ren Pa's Big Four...

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:42.950
How I've missed the sound of those words.

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:44.410
It's been three years, but:

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:47.430
"Gen Pou: One 
of Ren Pa's Big Four"

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:46.620
Gen Pou!

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:47.450
Sir!

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:50.430
"Kyou En: One 
of Ren Pa's Big Four"

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:49.660
Kyou En!

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:50.410
Sir.

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:52.540
Kai Shi Bou!

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.440
"Kai Shi Bou: One of 
Ren Pa's Big Four"

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:53.410
Sir!

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:55.330
Rin Ko!

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:56.440
"Rin Ko: One of
 Ren Pa's Big Four"

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:56.750
Yessir!

00:11:56.750 --> 00:12:00.370
You haven't gone all rusty on me, have you?

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:01.370
No, sir!

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:04.200
Rin Ko!

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.790
Ye-e-es?

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:07.290
You know the drill:

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:09.620
You go on ahead, find a promising enemy officer,

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.410
and bring me his head.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:14.330
Can you handle three thousand men?

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:17.200
That should be fine.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:21.250
My 300-man squadron will be
more than enough for a job like that!

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.970
"Ren Pa"

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.870
One month into the war,

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:33.290
and the Chin army's main Mou Gou camp

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:36.870
had begun their assault
on the third castle, Kin Rikan.

00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:42.870
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:51.000
Don't go climbing that siege tower! That's ours!

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:53.160
Shut it! This siege tower

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.040
belongs to all of us!

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.660
Why, you--

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:00.080
Yesss! We're on the wall!

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:04.500
Hi Shin Unit, onward!

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:07.750
Don't let the Gyoku Hou Force get all the glory!

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.450
You think we'll just keep
falling for this? Get them!

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:25.450
Shin!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.950
There are way more enemies than we'd expected!

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:33.410
It's the third castle, all right--
they're more than ready for us now!

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:36.250
This is tough even for us <i>and</i> the Gyoku Hou Force!

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:41.410
Hey! Down below! Yeah, you!

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:45.330
Quit standin' around and shimmy
up that siege tower already!

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:48.910
There's plenty of honor
to be won up on the castle wall!

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:58.500
Huh?!

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.040
S-Stop! Stay down!

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:04.660
That thing can only hold so many people!

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:08.620
And that is far too many! Stop at once!

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.080
You'll break it!

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.200
Well, wasn't <i>that</i> cinchy!

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.120
Mou Ten! Not you, too!

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.370
Watch out!

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:19.580
Here they come!

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:25.250
The heavy infantry...

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:27.040
Gyoku Hou Force, into formation!

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:30.040
Here we go! Your time to shine, fellas!

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:34.080
Now!

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:37.200
The Hi Shin Unit's Tremendous Triad--go!

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.580
Right! Force your way inside!

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:40.870
Got it!

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.830
Wow...

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:51.750
All it takes is experience,
and they're already markedly stronger

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.160
than those foot soldiers.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.000
On top of that,

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:12.370
their commander and lieutenant
have outstanding sword skills.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:13.790
Yes, the Hi Shin Unit:

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:19.330
Rough around the edges, maybe,
but their destructive power is no joke.

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:25.120
I guess Ou Ki didn't form
that special unit just for show, huh?

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:26.250
Still...

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:31.790
That lieutenant is a real piece of work.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.950
C'mon! Go go go!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:40.450
Eh? What are they doing?

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:42.830
They're moving directly
opposite from the stairs!

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:46.450
And they've got rope?!

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:49.950
D-Don't tell me they plan to copy our tactics!

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:54.370
You there! What are you doing?
Have you no pride?!

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:55.500
Shut up!

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:59.450
We take pride in not havin' any piss-poor pride!

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:03.080
Nonsense! What kind of pride is that?!

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:04.370
All right!

00:16:04.370 --> 00:16:06.790
Here we go, Ryuu Sen! Hold on tight!

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:09.450
Shin, wait a sec!

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:11.580
They already know about that tactic!

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:14.580
There are tons of soldiers waiting
in front of the castle gates!

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:19.000
I think even before they get that far...

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:26.160
Shin! You're off-course!

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:28.040
Huh?

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:31.040
That's not the top of the gates!

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:45.450
Ow!

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:59.370
Shiiin!

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.410
Idiot.

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:12.580
Oh! He moved!

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:15.200
He's alive! Shin's alive!

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.160
Ow ow ow...

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.500
Honestly!

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:25.000
He <i>would</i> be a force for the Gyoku Hou
and Gaku Ka to reckon with...

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.450
if he weren't such a dunce.

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:29.120
Still,

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:31.870
I guess that's part of what
makes 'em the Hi Shin Unit.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:37.450
Someone's fallen!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.200
Ow ow ow...

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.950
Kill him!

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:47.500
Uh-oh! Shin's a rat in a trap!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.540
Let's go, team!

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.910
Yeah, but how?

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:55.870
J-Just run away for now, Shin!

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:09.000
Those are Chin flags!

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.950
They've stormed the south wall!

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.330
When'd <i>that</i> happen?

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:19.540
The enemy sent extra troops
after that fancy siege tower,

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:22.330
so obviously the other units were shorthanded.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.870
Plus,

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.870
that's Kaku Bi's thousand-man unit,

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:33.040
which means skilled troops
as mighty as those in the main force.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.410
No time to be standin' and starin'!

00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:41.120
C'mon, guys! Get down here
before they steal our thunder!

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:47.450
Afterward, the castle-storming
Hi Shin Unit happened to run into

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:51.700
a renowned military officer...
and defeated him.

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:54.620
In the end, their achievements
were greater than those

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:57.040
of the Gyoku Hou and Gaku Ka Forces.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:05.120
Listen up!

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:09.290
We didn't get the general's head,
but never mind that--

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:10.700
let's celebrate!

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.160
Although luck certainly played a part,

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:18.700
the Hi Shin Unit was truly happy
with their first victory in a long while.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:24.200
Nice graceful fall you got there, commander!

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.370
Aw, shaddap!

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:28.200
Hey, where <i>is</i> that Ryuu Sen, anyway?
Get over here!

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:33.200
Leave it to Shin to come away
from that without a scratch!

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:37.620
And that siege tower!
The wheels were wrecked in the end!

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:40.370
Wrecked? No way!

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:43.620
Yeah, and that old Gyoku Hou guy
got all teary-eyed!

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.540
Serves 'em right!

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:50.790
Ah, so <i>that's</i> the Hi Shin Unit!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.540
Huh? Who's that?

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:01.040
Kaku Bi, sir, please hurry! The war council--

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:02.200
Kaku Bi?

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.700
I'll be right there. You go on ahead.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:07.120
Kaku Bi... isn't that the
thousand-man commander

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:08.450
who took the general's head today?

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.410
S-Shin...

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:12.410
Sir!

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:18.330
So you're Shin...

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:22.000
You look just as I'd imagined.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.910
You were once a servant, yes?

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:31.000
I've had something I've wanted
to tell you ever since I heard.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.950
Well? Out with it!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.790
I, Kaku Bi, was once a servant, too.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:44.620
Like you, I lost my parents to war.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:47.950
From a young age, I went from
house to house as a servant,

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:51.830
until a childless couple
took me in as their own.

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:55.370
Now I stand among the military elite.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:21:00.120
When I heard your circumstances,
I was reminded of my past.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:03.450
I have been rooting for you ever since.

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:11.500
To be a 300-man commander
with no outside support, and at your age?

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.160
You've really been working hard.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:16.040
N-No, I...

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:20.750
I also admired your attacking
Ran Dou at Gao Lang.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:21.750
Have you noticed?

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:28.080
Thanks to you, there've been almost
no such violations this time around.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:30.830
You did it, Shin!

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:31.830
Yeah!

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:41.000
Uh, hey, wait!

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:45.450
I thought I'd step in to offer my help, but...

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:48.330
...I see I should just mind my own business.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:53.870
This unit is on the right track.
Just keep going.

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:59.290
Don't let those nobles beat you, Shin!

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:05.910
Mou Ten was telling us.

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:09.660
Smarts, skills, spirit--Kaku Bi's got it all.

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:12.160
He's popular and extremely talented,

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:14.000
even for the Chin army.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:19.580
Out of all the young officers,
he's closest to becoming general.

00:22:19.580 --> 00:22:25.200
He was already one of Mou Gou's
closest advisors in this battle.

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:29.950
A thousand-man commander,
and already advising generals...

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:32.660
And he's still pretty young, too.

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:35.910
He sure didn't look like someone
who used to be a servant.

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:38.870
He was even grander than those noble types...

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:42.040
But so pleasant! Not nasty at all!

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:44.580
I guess there <i>are</i> people like that.

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:48.750
Kaku Bi... the thousand-man commander...

00:22:56.750 --> 00:22:59.370
Commander Kaku Bi, a moment?

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:15.580
Let's see...

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:18.830
Who's next?

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"The Air of a General"
